"The prognosis is driven by several factors, including a preoperative PSA of 8.6 and an ISUP grade group 3 (Gleason 4+4) from the prostatectomy specimen. Positive surgical margins are also concerning findings. Countervailing points include no documented seminal vesicle invasion and no lymph node metastasis reported in the surgical pathology. The biopsy-to-prostatectomy difference is noted as the Gleason pattern and ISUP report were missing for the initial biopsy session, while the prostatectomy provided a definitive grade of 4+4 (ISUP group 3). Missing information regarding postoperative PSA trajectory would significantly revise this prognosis. The fixed estimated horizon is 51.41 months. This represents expected follow-up without an event, not a known recurrence date. The sensitivity range is 41.13–61.69 months; its coverage has not been validated."
